    "summary": "Epic Weather Report Suite, soaring China>Rider, tight jam marathon",
    "blurb": "The show bursts with a fiery Weather Report Suite and a soaring China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider. The second set delivers an extended Other One jam, strong Truckin' > Nobody's Fault But Mine flow, and a heartfelt Wharf Rat. Overall the performance is high‑energy with standout vocals and tight rhythm.",
    "review": "On December 8 1973 at Cameron Indoor Stadium the Dead were in top form, delivering one of their most adventurous late‑’73 outings. The first set builds from crisp country‑rock numbers into a monumental Weather Report Suite (Prelude → Part 1 → Let It Grow) that showcases Jerry’s climactic guitar leads and Keith’s funk‑laden keyboards. A highlight is the seamless China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider segue, where Jerry’s “extra sweet” vocals ride Phil’s bass splurge. The second set ramps up the improvisational stakes: a powerful Other One stretch, a tight Truckin' → Nobody's Fault But Mine transition, and an emotive Wharf Rat that leads into a soulful Stella Blue encore before closing with One More Saturday Night. Across multiple soundboard sources the playing is consistently inspired, making this show a must‑listen for fans of the band’s late‑’73 peak.",
